-- Course: Master of Counselling and Psychotherapy (115903E)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This degree supports you to become a clinically proficient counsellor with a strong foundation in ethical and evidence based clinical competencies. You’ll explore contemporary theories and therapeutic approaches, learning to take a holistic approach to emotional, mental and relational challenges. You’ll build practical skills through hands-on experiential learning, including simulated scenarios with actors representing clients. </p><p>Develop cultural sensitivity to work safely and effectively with clients from diverse backgrounds. Strengthen your interpersonal and active listening skills, learning to build empathy and establish trust. Find out how to guide conversations and facilitate self-exploration. Across the degree, you’ll also gain unique insights into your own life and a deep understanding of your own personal growth. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    total_course_duration = '2 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 46700,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>A completed bachelor (AQF level 7) degree or equivalent from a recognised higher education institution</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Undertake the Casper Situational Judgement Test (CSJT)</li><li>Attend an interview, if invited</li><li>In cases where there are more eligible applicants than available places, admission will be competitive with ranks based on the entry criteria</li><li>Applications are considered on an individual basis and selection is competitive</li><li>Possession of English qualifications, in addition to academic entry requirements, does not guarantee a place</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, the application must be accompanied by certified documentation from the educational institution/employer certifying that the language of instruction/employment was English</li><li>IELTS Overall 7</li><li>IELTS Reading 7</li><li>IELTS Listening 7</li><li>IELTS Speaking 7</li><li>IELTS Writing 7</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
