-- Course: Graduate Diploma in International Business (115862J)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This graduate diploma is a one-year qualification that will teach you key international business concepts with a strong focus on the growing Asian markets. </p><p>Acquire practical and analytical skills, examining international trade, global supply chains and cross-cultural management. You’ll also gain an understanding on how international companies adapt their strategies to changing economic conditions and cultural expectations. </p><p>Your knowledge and skills will be applicable to a wide range of industries, particularly in roles involving global operations, cross-border transactions, international trade and multicultural environments. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    total_course_duration = '1 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 54900,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>A completed bachelor (AQF level 7) or bachelor honours (AQF level 8) degree or equivalent from a recognised higher education institution; OR</li><li>A completed nested or related graduate certificate (AQF level 8) or higher or equivalent from a recognised higher education institution; OR</li><li>A completed Advanced Diploma (AQF level 6) or higher in a related field from a registered training organisation (RTO).</li><li>In cases where there are more eligible applicants than available places, admission will be competitive with ranks based on the entry criteria.</li><li>Applications are considered on an individual basis and selection is competitive.</li><li>Possession of one or more of these qualifications, in addition to the academic entry requirements, does not, in itself, guarantee a place at Adelaide University.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission.</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, the application must be accompanied by certified documentation from the educational institution/employer certifying that the language of instruction/employment was English.</li><li>IELTS Overall 6.5</li><li>IELTS Reading 6</li><li>IELTS Listening 6</li><li>IELTS Speaking 6</li><li>IELTS Writing 6</li><li>Please access the following link for a comprehensive list of English language tests accepted by Adelaide University and other important information in relation to meeting the University’s language requirements: Equivalent English qualifications</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/graduate-diploma-in-international-business/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '115862J';

-- Course: Graduate Certificate in Project Management (115824D)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Build a versatile skillset that’s globally in-demand with our Graduate Certificate in Project Management. </p><p>From construction and healthcare to software development and marketing, project-based work models are fast becoming the norm in many industries. In this graduate certificate, you’ll be introduced to the key theories and practices necessary for managing projects across various stages of the project lifecycle.</p><p>Explore a wide range of principles, skills and techniques including project management methodologies and concepts, processes and techniques – and how these can be applied within a project environment. Learn best-practice approaches to risk management, including how to identify and treat risks early, and tools for addressing risks at each stage of the project lifecycle. Examine effective approaches to project leadership and stakeholder management through interactive case studies and practical content. Gain knowledge of key project control techniques for managing linear and non-complex projects, alongside skills in cost, time and contract management. </p><p>You’ll emerge with a versatile skillset, ready to contribute in project management-based roles in a variety of industry sectors. </p><p>Additionally, successful completion of this course can be credited towards our Master of Project Management. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 26,
    total_course_duration = '0.5 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 252500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>A completed bachelor (AQF level 7) or bachelor honours (AQF level 8) degree or equivalent from a recognised higher education institution; OR</li><li>A minimum of five years relevant work experience.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission:</li><li>IELTS Overall 6.5</li><li>IELTS Reading 6</li><li>IELTS Listening 6</li><li>IELTS Speaking 6</li><li>IELTS Writing 6</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, the application must be accompanied by certified documentation from the educational institution/employer certifying that the language of instruction/employment was English.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>In cases where there are more eligible applicants than available places, admission will be competitive with ranks based on the entry criteria.</li><li>Possession of one or more of these qualifications, in addition to the academic entry requirements, does not, in itself, guarantee a place at Adelaide University.</li><li>Applications are considered on an individual basis and selection is competitive.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/graduate-certificate-in-project-management/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '115824D';

-- Course: Graduate Diploma in Technology, Innovation and Entrepreneurship (115882E)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>The Graduate Diploma in Technology, Innovation and Entrepreneurship empowers you to become a catalyst for transformative change in the fast-paced world of technology driven business. Gain the cross-disciplinary expertise to bridge the gap between visionary ideas and real-world impact.</p><p>Immerse yourself in cutting-edge innovation concepts and entrepreneurial strategies. Develop the expertise to identify emerging technologies and translate them into market-ready solutions. Develop your skills in data analytics, ethical decision-making and persuasive communication.</p><p>You''ll master the art of strategic innovation management, learn to navigate complex commercialisation pathways and lead groundbreaking projects from idea through to implementation.</p><p>Graduate prepared to drive the future of technology and business, equipped to make a lasting impact across industries. Be at the forefront of innovation, shaping a more dynamic and sustainable future.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    total_course_duration = '1 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 50500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
