-- Course: Bachelor of Laws (Honours), Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice (117414F)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This degree prepares you for rewarding careers influencing systems and improving lives. </p><p>Gain a deep understanding of the law – and how and why laws change over time. Research past decisions to understand precedent and learn to analyse and interpret laws, regulations and court rulings. </p><p>Harness your problem-solving skills to navigate legal matters and advocate for the rights of your clients. </p><p>Through your studies in criminology and criminal justice, you’ll uncover the complex causes and nature of crime and its impact on society. Examine the way we respond to crime and consider strategies for intervention. </p><p>In just five years, you’ll earn a double degree and an Honours qualification, allowing you to pursue careers in the legal and corporate sectors, government, law enforcement, corrections services and more*. </p><p>*To be admitted to legal practice, you’ll need to fulfil the practical requirements for admission, which includes completion of the Graduate Diploma in Legal Practice. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 260,
    total_course_duration = '5 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 54900,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>Completion of secondary education equivalent to South Australian Certificate of Education (SACE)</li><li>Successful completion of at least 6 months full-time study (or equivalent part-time) in an undergraduate diploma (AQF level 5) or higher</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>IELTS Overall 7, Reading 7, Listening 7, Speaking 7, Writing 7</li><li>International students with English as an additional language must provide certified documentation from educational institution/employer confirming English as language of instruction/employment</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Admission is competitive with ranks based on entry criteria</li><li>Possession of listed qualifications does not guarantee admission</li><li>Country-specific requirements (e.g., Australia ATAR 85, Bangladesh HSC 4.95, etc.)</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-laws-honours-bachelor-of-criminology-and-criminal-justice/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '117414F';

-- Course: Bachelor of Science (Veterinary Bioscience) (115754B)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Learn about the world of animals and train in the ways you can care for them. Explore the anatomy, physiology and behaviour of healthy animals while also identifying the pathogenic organisms that attack them. Your studies will give you an insight into animal handling and husbandry and you’ll have opportunities to experience real industry settings including farms and production facilities.</p><p>This practical degree offers a significant amount of hands-on animal work, starting from your first semester. You’ll have access to purpose-built veterinary teaching and research facilities to help you learn job ready skills and techniques.</p><p>This degree is the first part of Adelaide University’s six year veterinary science program and graduates can gain direct entry into the Doctor of Veterinary Medicine. Upon completing both degrees, you’ll be eligible to register as a veterinarian.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    total_course_duration = '3 year(s) full-time only (no part time option)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 59300,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>Admission is competitive; eligible applicants considered based on Questionnaire and Acuity Insights assessment (Casper) results</li><li>Secondary education: Completion of qualification equivalent to SACE with adjusted ATAR equivalent selection rank of 90.00 or higher</li><li>Higher education study: Successful completion of at least 6 months full-time (or equivalent part-time) in AQF level 5+ undergraduate diploma or higher with GPA 5.0 or higher</li><li>International admissions by country with specified qualification and score: Australia ATAR 90; Bangladesh HSC 4.97; Canada OSSD 85%; China Gaokao 80%; Denmark stx 7 (Good); France French Baccalaureate 13.5; Global IB 33; Hong Kong HKDSE 21; India CBSE and CISCE 85; India State Board 98; Indonesia SMA III 90%; Kenya KCSE A-; Malaysia Matrikulasi 3.33; Malaysia STPM 3.33; Malaysia UEC 11; Nepal NEB 3.61; Norway Upper Secondary School Certificate 4.8; Philippines High School Diploma K12 94%; Singapore GCE A Levels 12; South Korea CSAT 355; Sri Lanka GCE A Levels 12; Sweden Upper Secondary School Leaving Certificate 16.0; Taiwan GSAT 80%; Thailand Matayom 6 3.90; UK/Global GCE A Levels 12; USA/Global AP 12; USA/Global ACT 29; USA/Global SAT 1280; Vietnam Year 12 8.7</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as additional language must meet one standard within last two years prior to admission</li><li>IELTS Overall 7, Reading 7, Listening 7, Speaking 7, Writing 7</li><li>Equivalent English qualifications accepted — see Adelaide University link</li><li>Where previous study/work in English, application must include certified documentation of English instruction/employment</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Complete prescribed questionnaire about life experiences and knowledge/interest in veterinary science</li><li>Complete Acuity Insights assessment (Casper)</li><li>Read, understand and believe you will meet Inherent Requirements</li><li>Read, understand and agree to Vaccination Guidelines</li><li>Possession of qualifications in addition to academic entry does not guarantee place; applications considered individually; selection competitive</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-science-veterinary-bioscience/',
    updated_at = NOW()
