-- Course: Bachelor of Medical Studies (115733G)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>The Bachelor of Medical Studies provides foundational knowledge and skills needed to excel in health care. You’ll learn from outstanding clinicians in state-of-the-art facilities and develop a deep understanding of how our health care system works. You’ll also gain a valuable ‘consumer’ perspective, helping you understand how patients interact with health services and providers.</p><p>During your studies you’ll explore scenario-based problems, focussing on individual, community, Indigenous and global health issues. You’ll also gain valuable exposure to real-world clinical practice and develop safe and effective clinical skills in cutting-edge simulation facilities.</p><p>This degree is the first three years of the Adelaide University''s six-year integrated medicine program, and upon successful completion you’ll gain direct entry into the Doctor of Medicine. Together, these degrees will qualify you to practise as an intern anywhere in Australia and throughout most of the world.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    total_course_duration = '3 year(s) full-time only (no part time option)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 99000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>Admission is competitive; applicants must meet at least one minimum entry requirement, demonstrate prerequisites, sit UCAT ANZ, and attend interview if invited.</li><li>Secondary education (Year 12): Completion of qualification equivalent to SACE with adjusted ATAR equivalent selection rank of 90.00 or higher.</li><li>Higher education study: Must have successfully completed at least one year and no more than two years full-time (or equivalent part-time) in bachelor (AQF 7) or bachelor honours (AQF 8) or equivalent.</li><li>Higher education study: Only tertiary record must be from Adelaide University or antecedent institutions (University of Adelaide or University of South Australia); no other Australian or overseas university record (excluding accelerated Year 12 such as activate program).</li><li>Higher education study: Must meet program prerequisite requirements (secondary or equivalent university courses).</li><li>Higher education study: Students with more than two years undergraduate study or any third-year courses not eligible; consider graduate medicine.</li><li>First year students (Adelaide University): 36-48 units Level 1 study, credit average GPA 5.0+ across all courses.</li><li>Second year students (Adelaide University): 72-96 units Level 1 and 2 study, credit average GPA 5.0+ across all courses.</li><li>First year students (University of Adelaide): 18-24 units Level 1 study, credit average GPA 5.0+ across all courses.</li><li>Second year students (University of Adelaide): 24-48 units Level 1 and 2 study, credit average GPA 5.0+ across all courses.</li><li>First year students (University of South Australia): 27-36 units Level 1 study, credit average GPA 5.0+ across all courses.</li><li>Second year students (University of South Australia): 36-72 units Level 1 and 2 study, credit average GPA 5.0+ across all courses.</li><li>Student exiting with Bachelor of Medical Studies conferred not eligible to re-enter Doctor of Medicine program.</li><li>Australia ATAR 90</li><li>Bangladesh Higher Secondary Certificate (HSC) 4.97</li><li>Canada Ontario Secondary School Diploma (OSSD) 85%</li><li>China Gaokao 80%</li><li>Denmark Studentereksamen (stx: Upper Secondary School Diploma) 7 (Good)</li><li>France French Baccalaureate 13.5</li><li>Global International Baccalaureate 33</li><li>Hong Kong Diploma of Secondary Education (HKDSE) 21</li><li>India CBSE and CISCE 85</li><li>India State Board Examinations 98</li><li>Indonesia SMA III 90%</li><li>Kenya Certificate of Secondary Education (KCSE) A-</li><li>Malaysia Matrikulasi 3.33</li><li>Malaysia Sijil Tinggi Persekolahan Malaysia (STPM) 3.33</li><li>Malaysia United Entrance Certificate (UEC) 11</li><li>Nepal National Examinations Board (NEB) 3.61</li><li>Norway Upper Secondary School Certificate (Vitnemal fra den Videregaende Skole) / Vitnemal For Videregaende Opplaering 4.8</li><li>Phillippines High School Diploma (Grade 12) (Academic Track) K12 94%</li><li>Singapore Singapore GCE Advanced Levels 12</li><li>South Korea College Scholastic Ability Test (CSAT) 355</li><li>Sri Lanka GCE A Levels 12</li><li>Sweden Upper Secondary School Leaving Certificate 16.0</li><li>Taiwan GSAT % 80%</li><li>Thailand Matayom 6 3.90</li><li>UK / Global GCE Advanced Levels 12</li><li>USA / Global Advanced Placement (AP) 12</li><li>USA / Global America College Test (ACT) 29</li><li>USA / Global Scholastic Assessment Test (SAT) 1280</li><li>Vietnam Bằng Tốt Nghiệp Trung Học Phổ Thông (Vietnamese Year 12) 8.7</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within last two years prior to admission.</li><li>IELTS Overall 7, Reading 7, Listening 7, Speaking 7, Writing 7.</li><li>Previous study/work in English must be accompanied by certified documentation from institution/employer certifying English was language of instruction/employment.</li><li>Equivalent English qualifications link provided by Adelaide University.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>University Clinical Aptitude Test (UCAT ANZ) must be sat.</li><li>Interview must be attended if invited.</li><li>If academic minimum met, selected for interview on basis of UCAT ANZ results.</li><li>Eligible applicants ranked on combination of UCAT ANZ, interview, and academic score results.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-medical-studies/',
    updated_at = NOW()
